2026-09-06T00:00Z claude note Imagine phase (raid, sonnet): PROCEED, but the six-row table alone is not sufficient -- necessary but not sufficient against this ticket's own "no jargon outside diagnostics" intent. Gaps found by reading bootstrap.js directly: (1) the toolbar tooltip leaks raw internal phase strings verbatim when phase isn't 'census' (e.g. 'native-worker-busy', 'low-memory', 'launch-declined; disable/re-enable to launch') -- none in the table; (2) the global status line 'Packs a jour : X / Y' uses the excluded word 'packs' but isn't literally named by any checkbox; (3) 'active document' needs new plumbing, not a word swap -- state.active is a raw item ID today, never a title (title is already computed in inspect() as result.title and needs threading through); (4) 'finished with exceptions' is a new summary line, not a rename -- nothing today surfaces failures outside the diagnostics block. All four must land in the same pass or the checkboxes will read green while the leak is only half-fixed. Also: pair the sitter's own 'index' rename with Zotero's native full-text panel rename in the same commit (acceptance criterion 2 already requires this; the collision doesn't exist yet but a partial implementation would create it).
2026-09-06T00:00Z claude note Author directive 1 (PR #369 review): "Informative tooltip is nice to have, preserve." Dropping the phase word outside 'census' fixed the raw-name leak but cost all zero-click observability -- a blocked sitter read exactly like a healthy idle one. Resolved with SDT_PHASE_LABELS: a plain French sentence per blocking/error phase, an explicit null for the two healthy idle phases, bare count for anything unlisted. Added acceptance line 4.
2026-09-06T00:00Z claude note Author directive 2 (PR #369 review): "document" is banned from the UI, not merely imprecise. The sitter indexes attachments (SELECT itemID FROM itemAttachments; Zotero.SDT.ensure(attachmentID)) and a reference can carry several (SPEC.md D6); Zotero's own French UI renders *item* as "document", so the word named the wrong object. Vocabulary gains file/fichier and reference; "document", "element", "piece jointe", "item" join the banned list. The directive also exposed a real defect: inspect() sets title from the attachment's own field, which Zotero auto-generates ("Full Text PDF"), so the threaded title identified nothing -- parentTitle now threads alongside it and the active line composes reference then file. Added acceptance line 3.
2026-09-06T00:00Z claude note Downstream, not re-planned here: 0693/0696/0699 need the same reference-then-file composition and the "document" ban; 0692's Fluent ids should read files-indexed / files-failed. One residual ambiguity reported, not changed: the extraction plateau message "Analyse des references..." uses "references" in its bibliographic sense, which now collides with "reference" as the parent item -- rewording it needs a ruling on what the processor is actually doing at that point.
2026-09-06T00:00Z claude note Consistency review round 3 (PR #369): describeError still led with the attachment's auto-generated title and appended the reference -- the same defect just fixed on the progress line, at a site this PR had already touched for the word swap. Root cause was two independent compositions, so both now go through one describeSDTFile(info, fallback) and a test asserts neither site composes its own label. Also: BANNED_IN_UI had drifted from the ban this ticket states ("item" missing), and the quietMessage strings were outside the checked site list; both closed.
